(* ============================================================
   radical.ebnf — a second, Clojure-flavored grammar for the musics
   DSL, alongside musics.ebnf (which stays the LilyPond-superset
   grammar, unchanged, untouched by anything in this file).
   ============================================================

   Leaf syntax — notes, chords, rests, drums, pitches, durations,
   articulation, ornaments, dynamics, hairpins, ties, slurs — is
   IDENTICAL to musics.ebnf: absolute/relative pitch resolution,
   octave ticks, everything at that level is untouched, copied as-is.
   What changes is everything above the leaf: container brackets now
   mirror core.async-engine's own play-arg mini-language (a Clojure
   vector is sequential, a Clojure set is parallel — see that
   namespace's own docstring) instead of LilyPond's own { }/<< >>, and
   the transient structural commands (times/tuplet/transpose/repeat/
   grace) read as ordinary Lisp prefix calls instead of backslash-
   keywords.

   Motivated by input.lilypond-import now being a real, actively-
   maintained LilyPond -> musics-text converter (see the project root
   CLAUDE.md) — this grammar no longer needs to double as a LilyPond
   superset the way musics.ebnf still deliberately is, so every
   concession that existed purely for that reason is free to go.

   Bracket system:
     [ ]      Sequence     musical sequence — also reused as-is for
                             times/tuplet/transpose/repeat's own body
                             and a VarDef's value, same "walker decides
                             registered vs. spliced/stashed by WHERE a
                             Sequence sits, never by how it's spelled"
                             principle musics.ebnf already uses
     #{ }     Parallel     simultaneous parts
     { }      Context      named context / envelope definition — a
                             genuine Clojure map-literal echo, since a
                             Context really is just a bag of key/value
                             settings, unlike musics.ebnf's own ^{ }
     '[ ]     Data         data container — reclaims its own, earlier
                             documented spelling (see musics.ebnf's
                             AtomicAlgo comment) from before algorithms
                             existed in either grammar
     ( )      also a slur mark glued directly onto a Note/Chord (c4( d4
                             e4)), exactly as in musics.ebnf — never
                             ambiguous with a prefix command call below,
                             since a slur's ( is always glued with no
                             separator onto an existing note/chord,
                             never a fresh element of its own; nor with
                             StructValue's own unrelated ( ) (a
                             parenthesized Value after !name:), reached
                             only from a totally different position —
                             three uses of one bracket, disambiguated
                             entirely by WHERE each is reachable, same
                             "position decides meaning" principle
                             musics.ebnf already relies on elsewhere

   Dropped entirely, not carried over from musics.ebnf:
     Unit ('{ }) — a plain [ ] Sequence covers the same grouping need;
       nothing here needed a context-less variant of its own to earn a
       whole separate bracket.
     AtomicAlgo (@[ ]) / ElementAlgo (@{ }) — grammar-native algorithm
       invocation. Reconsidered directly, not dropped lightly: almost
       everything under algo/ was already unwired from any grammar
       entry point, and the two registered examples (colorTalea, split)
       are just as reachable as plain Clojure functions called from the
       REPL. Parameterized playback algorithms now live entirely on the
       play/core.wall side (assign-algo!/configure-wall!), never in
       text, on either grammar.
     \time/\tempo/\key — LilyPond's own free-standing spellings for
       !Meter:/!tempo:/!key:, added to musics.ebnf purely so that
       grammar doubled as a closer LilyPond superset. !Meter:/!tempo:/
       !key: (Assignment/KeyAssignment) are unaffected and remain the
       only spelling here — dropping the alternates also frees "time",
       "tempo", "key" from VarName's own exclusion list, see below.

   repeat/tremolo: musics.ebnf keeps these as two separate rules that
   happen to share the \repeat keyword (tremolo = \repeat tremolo N
   { ... }). Here they're one rule, repeat-type (unfold/volta/tremolo)
   picking the variant — musics.ebnf's tremolo already required a
   Sequence body specifically, unlike unfold/volta's own looser bare
   Element (a known, documented gap between what the grammar allowed
   and what the walker actually handled); merging onto Sequence
   uniformly for all three closes that gap as a direct side effect,
   not a separately-decided change.

   Id/Reference/VarDef/VarRef, Instructions (!key:value, Ramps,
   \partial), and every leaf rule below are otherwise identical to
   musics.ebnf — see that file's own header comment and inline
   comments for the reasoning behind the parts this file doesn't
   repeat.

   Comments: ; to end of line (real Clojure, replacing musics.ebnf's
   own %-line form), %{ ... %} for a block (Clojure has no block-
   comment reader syntax of its own to borrow, so this one stays from
   musics.ebnf rather than being dropped along with the rest of the
   LilyPond-conformity concessions — it was never really about
   LilyPond specifically, just a delimiter, and losing the capability
   outright wasn't worth it just for symmetry).
   ============================================================ *)

(* Same reasoning as musics.ebnf's own TopElement: every alternative
   NOT listed here can write directly into whatever context is on top
   of the builder stack, which at Program's own top level is :ROOT --
   meant to be a read-only endpoint. repeat is the one exception kept
   reachable directly: an Iterator's own :source/:alternative is a
   real, retained container with a genuine context of its own, exactly
   as safe at top level as any other real container -- tremolo no
   longer needs its own separate mention here, it's a repeat-type now,
   not a sibling rule. *)
Program = ws? (TopElement (ws TopElement)*)? ws?
<TopElement> = Composite | repeat | VarDef

<Element> = Part | Instruction | Command

<Part> = Composite | Leaf | Reference | VarRef
<Leaf> = Chord | Note | Rest | Drum | MultiRest

(* Bar / section markers -- unchanged from musics.ebnf, unrelated to
   any bracket choice above. *)
BarLine = #'\|{1,4}'
<BarRun> = BarLine (ws? BarLine)*
<Sep> = ws
      | ws? BarRun ws?
<EdgeBar> = ws? BarRun ws?

(* ── Composites ─────────────────────────────────────────── *)

<Composite> = Context | Sequence | Parallel | Data

Context     = <'{'>  ws? (Id ws)?  Instruction (ws Instruction)* ws? <'}'>
            | <'{'>  ws? (Id ws)                                 ws? <'}'>

Sequence    = <'['>  ws? (Id ws)? EdgeBar? Element (Sep Element)* EdgeBar? ws? <']'>
            | <'['>  ws? (Id ws)                                          ws? <']'>

(* ParElement's alternatives (Context/Sequence/Reference/Instruction/
   Command) all start with a distinctive non-alphanumeric character
   ({ [ : ! \ (), so two of them can sit directly adjacent with no
   separator at all -- Sep is optional here, not just the bar line
   covered by EdgeBar. *)
Parallel    = <'#{'> ws? (Id ws)? EdgeBar? ParElement (Sep? ParElement)* EdgeBar? ws? <'}'>
            | <'#{'> ws? (Id ws)                                                 ws? <'}'>

Data        = <"'["> ws? (type ws)? (DataElement (ws DataElement)*)? ws? <']'>
type        = Name

<ParElement> = Context | Sequence | Reference | Instruction | Command | VarRef

(* DataElement: element for data containers *)
<ExtendedDataElement> = Atom | Primitive | Keyword | Name
<DataElement>         = Atom | Primitive
<Atom>                = Pitch | Duration | BareDuration | Articulation | BangConst | StringLit
<Primitive>           = Ratio | Float | Int

(* ── Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────── *)
(* Every one of these used to be a backslash-keyword taking bare
   juxtaposed args (\times 2/3 { ... }); now they're all ordinary Lisp
   prefix calls, ( verb args... body ). The verb itself is hidden
   ( <'times'> etc.) wherever the rule name alone already disambiguates
   it (times/tuplet/transpose/alternative each have their own distinct
   rule) -- but kept VISIBLE, untagged, wherever several variants share
   one rule and the word is the only way to tell them apart (repeat's
   own repeat-type, and grace's five near-identical shapes below),
   exactly the same "hide only what's redundant with the tag" choice
   musics.ebnf's own <repeat-type> already makes. *)

transpose   = <'('> ws? <'transpose'> ws from-pitch ws to-pitch ws Sequence ws? <')'>
from-pitch  = Pitch
to-pitch    = Pitch

times       = <'('> ws? <'times'>  ws multiply-factor ws Sequence ws? <')'>
tuplet      = <'('> ws? <'tuplet'> ws divide-factor   ws Sequence ws? <')'>
multiply-factor = Ratio
divide-factor   = Ratio

repeat       = <'('> ws? <'repeat'> ws repeat-type ws count ws Sequence (ws alternative)? ws? <')'>
<repeat-type> = 'volta' | 'unfold' | 'tremolo'
count        = Int
alternative  = <'('> ws? <'alternative'> ws Sequence ws? <')'>

(* Grace Notes -- same five forms, same two-Element/order-differs-by-
   keyword shape as musics.ebnf, just ( )-called instead of \-called.
   Order differs by keyword:
     grace/acciaccatura/appoggiatura/slashedGrace  -- grace-note main-note
     afterGrace                                    -- main-note grace-note *)
grace = <'('> ws? 'grace'        ws Element ws Element ws? <')'>
      | <'('> ws? 'acciaccatura' ws Element ws Element ws? <')'>
      | <'('> ws? 'appoggiatura' ws Element ws Element ws? <')'>
      | <'('> ws? 'slashedGrace' ws Element ws Element ws? <')'>
      | <'('> ws? 'afterGrace'   ws Element ws Element ws? <')'>

<Command> = transpose | times | tuplet | repeat | grace

(* ── Variables ──────────────────────────────────────────── *)
(* Unchanged mechanism from musics.ebnf: name = [ ... ] defines a
   variable (Sequence's own new [ ] bracket, reused as-is, same "walked
   and stashed, not registered" walk-time distinction musics.ebnf's own
   VarDef already relies on), \name references it, must be defined
   first. See src/input/CLAUDE.md's "Comments and variables" section
   for the full reasoning -- nothing about the MECHANISM changed here,
   only VarName's own exclusion list, which SHRANK: *)
VarDef = VarName ws? <'='> ws? Sequence
VarRef = <'\\'> VarName

(* Ornament names are the ONLY reserved words left -- \trill (Ornament)
   still shares VarRef's own \name spelling, the one remaining
   collision. times/tuplet/transpose/repeat/alternative/grace and its
   four synonyms no longer need excluding at all: they're ( )-prefixed
   commands now, sharing nothing with \name's own spelling, so there's
   no ambiguity left to guard against. time/tempo/key don't need
   excluding either -- \time/\tempo/\key don't exist in this grammar,
   so there's nothing left for a variable named that to collide with. *)
VarName = #'(?!(prallmordent|prallprall|lineprall|prallup|pralldown|downprall|prall|upmordent|downmordent|mordent|trill|turn|reverseturn|verylongfermata|longfermata|shortfermata|fermata)\b)[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*'

(* ── Instructions ───────────────────────────────────────── *)
(* Entirely unchanged from musics.ebnf, Time/Tempo/Key dropped (see the
   header comment) and nothing else touched. *)

<Instruction> = BangConst | KeyAssignment | Assignment | Invalidate | Partial

Partial = <'\\partial'> ws Duration

BangConst     = <'!'> Name
KeyAssignment = <'!key:'> KeySpec
Assignment    = <'!'> AssignName Ramp
              | <'!'> AssignName <':'> Value RampMark?

AssignName = #'(?!key\b)[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*'
Invalidate    = <'!/'> Name

<Value> = TempoMark | Ratio | SignedFloat | SignedInt | StringLit | QualifiedName | StructValue

TempoMark = (Int | Ratio) <'='> Int

(* ── Ramp ───────────────────────────────────────────────── *)
(* Unchanged from musics.ebnf -- see that file's own extensive comment
   on Ramp's four shapes if the details are needed; nothing here
   depends on any bracket/command choice above. *)

Ramp         = RampMark
             | Direction              DurationExpr <':'> Target
             | Direction CurvePrefix <':'> DurationExpr <':'> Target

<RampMark>   = Direction CurvePrefix?

DurationExpr = DurationAtom (<'*'> DurationAtom)*
DurationAtom = Ratio | Int

Target       = DynamicMark | SignedFloat | SignedInt

DynamicMark  = 'pppp' | 'ppp' | 'pp' | 'p' | 'mp' | 'mf'
             | 'ffff' | 'fff' | 'ff' | 'f'

(* StructValue keeps musics.ebnf's own ( ) -- see the header comment's
   bracket-system note on why this never collides with a slur or a
   command call, despite all three now sharing the same bracket. *)
StructValue   = <'('> ws? (ExtendedDataElement (ws ExtendedDataElement)*)? ws? <')'>
QualifiedName = Name (<'.'> Name)*
KeySpec       = #'[A-Ga-g][b#]?(?:\.[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)*'

<CurvePrefix> = 'l' | 's' | 'i' | 'o'
<Direction>   = '<' | '>'

(* ── Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────── *)
(* Everything from here to the end of Primitives is IDENTICAL to
   musics.ebnf, copied as-is -- leaf syntax is explicitly out of scope
   for this grammar's own redesign. See musics.ebnf's own inline
   comments for the reasoning behind each of these rules. *)

Note  = Pitch Duration Articulation? NoteSuffix*
      | Pitch           Articulation? NoteSuffix*

Pitch          = PitchLetterAbs Accidental? OctaveAbs?
               | PitchLetterRel Accidental? OctaveTicks?
PitchLetterAbs = #'[A-G]'
PitchLetterRel = #'[a-gp]'

Accidental  = #'isis|eses|ses|ss|ff|is|es|s|f|x|##|bb|[#bn]'

<Octave>    = OctaveAbs | OctaveTicks
OctaveAbs   = #'[1-8](?:/|(?!\d))'
OctaveTicks = #"'+|,+"

(* ── Duration ───────────────────────────────────────────── *)

<Duration>      = DurationSpecial | DurationNum
DurationSpecial = #'\\longa' | #'\\breve'
DurationNum     = #'[1-9][0-9]{0,2}\.*'

BareDuration    = <'/'> Duration

(* ── Articulation ───────────────────────────────────────── *)

Articulation          = <'-'> ArticulationShorthand
                      | <#'\\'> ArticulationName
ArticulationName      = 'staccato' | 'staccatissimo' | 'tenuto' | 'marcato' |
                        'portato'  | 'accent'         | 'espressivo'
ArticulationShorthand = #'[-.>^_!+]'

(* ── Modifiers, Ornaments, Tremolo ──────────────────────── *)

OrnamentName = 'prall'     | 'prallup'      | 'pralldown'   | 'upprall'     |
               'downprall' | 'prallprall'   | 'lineprall'   | 'prallmordent'|
               'mordent'   | 'upmordent'    | 'downmordent' |
               'trill'     | 'turn'         | 'reverseturn' |
               'shortfermata' | 'fermata'   | 'longfermata' | 'verylongfermata'

Ornament = <#'\\'> OrnamentName
Modifier = <#'\\'> Name <':'> ModValue
Tremolo  = <':'> Int

Dynamic  = <#'\\'> DynamicMark Direction?

Hairpin  = <#'\\'> ('<' | '>')

<ModValue>   = Float | Int | StringLit | Name

<NoteSuffix> = Modifier | Ornament | Dynamic | Hairpin | Tremolo | SlurMark | Tie

SlurMark = '(' | ')'

(* ── Tie ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── *)

Tie = '~'

(* ── Chord ───────────────────────────────────────────────── *)

Chord = '<' !'<' ChordPitches '>' Duration Articulation? NoteSuffix*
      | '<' !'<' ChordPitches '>'          Articulation? NoteSuffix*

<ChordPitches> = Pitch ws Pitch (ws Pitch)*

(* ── Rest ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *)

Rest = 'r' Duration
     | 'r'

(* ── MultiRest ───────────────────────────────────────────── *)

MultiRest = 'R' Duration <'*'> Int
          | 'R' Duration
          | 'R' <'*'> Int
          | 'R'

(* ── Drum ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *)

Drum    = 'x' Duration DrumMod?
        | 'x'          DrumMod?
DrumMod = <#'\\'> (Int | Name)

(* ── Primitives ──────────────────────────────────────────── *)

Name        = #'[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*'
Float       = #'[0-9]+\.[0-9]+'
Int         = #'[0-9]+'
Ratio       = #'[0-9]+/[0-9]+'
SignedFloat = #'[+-]?[0-9]+\.[0-9]+'
SignedInt   = #'[+-]?[0-9]+'
StringLit = <'"'> #'[^"]*' <'"'>
Keyword   = <':'> #'[a-zA-Z0-9_][a-zA-Z0-9_\-]*'
Id        = Name <':'>
Reference = <':'> Name

(* ── Whitespace and comments ────────────────────────────── *)
(* ; to end of line replaces musics.ebnf's own %-line form (real
   Clojure line comments, no negative-lookahead trick needed the way
   musics.ebnf's own %(?!\{) required -- ; and %{ don't share a leading
   character, so there's nothing for the two alternatives to compete
   over). %{ ... %} block form kept unchanged, see the header comment. *)
Comment = #'%\{[\s\S]*?%\}'
        | #';[^\n]*'
<Blank> = #'\s+'
<ws>    = (Blank | Comment)+
